This design strategy should take into consideration only durable products that are able to endure many reuse process and therefore are truly circular. Increasing use through different loops will lower the total impacts of the product on the environment and facilitate the circulation of products. However, the geographical location where the cleanings methods may takes place should be considerate. Designers should explore this strategy through accurate evaluation of the business model. This strategy allows the use of products as far as possible, reducing the ammount of waste and prevents the need to harvest new raw materials.